title = "One block, three engines"
chapter = "4 / 7"
===

# {{title}} {#d-top}

A `data` block holds structured values. The `format=` names which syntax the
body is in, and the processor parses it, checks it, and makes it addressable —
it is not an opaque string that happens to look like config.

## json {#d-json}

=== data {#d-limits format=json}
{
  "maxDepth": 8,
  "timeoutMs": 2000,
  "allowRemote": false
}
===

Depth is capped at [[#d-limits["maxDepth"]]], with a
[[#d-limits["timeoutMs"]]] ms timeout.

## jsonl — one record per line {#d-jsonl}

=== data {#d-latency format=jsonl caption="p95 latency samples"}
{"region": "us", "p95": 41}
{"region": "eu", "p95": 58}
{"region": "ap", "p95": 96}
===

=== diagram {#d-latency-chart format=geml-chart data=#d-latency type=bar x=region y=p95 caption="p95 by region — charted from the jsonl above, by reference"}
===

The chart copies nothing. It names [[#d-latency]], and the column names are
checked when the document is parsed — rename `p95` in the data and the chart
fails the build instead of drawing an empty axis.

## yaml — new in 1.10.0, and deliberately a subset {#d-yaml}

=== data {#d-service format=yaml}
service: geml
retries: 3
enabled: true
endpoints:
  - name: primary
    port: 443
  - name: fallback
    port: 8443
===

The primary endpoint listens on [[#d-service["endpoints"][0]["port"]]] and the
fallback on [[#d-service["endpoints"][1]["port"]]].

=== note {.warning #d-subset}
Full YAML is not supported, on purpose. The places YAML is large are the places
implementations disagree — `yes` is a boolean in 1.1 and a string in 1.2, plus
anchors, tags, merge keys, multi-document streams. The engine reads block
collections nested by indentation, plain and quoted and block scalars, comments,
one document, `[]`/`{}`, with YAML 1.2 **core-schema** scalars — and **refuses
the rest by name** rather than guessing. A subset that means the same thing in
every processor beats a superset that means something different in each.
===

=== note {.tip #d-canon}
Canonical serialization is defined for `json` and `jsonl` only. Every other
format is byte-preserved, so `--to geml` will never rewrite your YAML into JSON
behind your back.
===
